<title>USA: Pennsylvania gas tax increase bill still in limbo.</title>
<headline>Pennsylvania gas tax increase bill still in limbo.</headline>
<dateline>HARRISBURG 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gov. Tom Ridge's gas tax proposal is in legislative limbo, with no formal plan in writing and House leaders saying there is still more work to be done on the issue.</p>
<p>Ridge is asking for a 3.5 cent hike in the cost of gas and a $12 bump in registration fees, arguing that the funds are needed for the state's crumbling highway system.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
